APEX Core: A Constrained Hamiltonian Manifold Formulation for Frictionless Rotor Dynamics and Autonomous Zero-Drag Control
Author: C. Matthew Blackwell, Independent Designer & Systems Architect, Lafayette, Louisiana
Abstract
This white sheet establishes a rigorous theoretical and operational framework for absolute mechanical friction elimination in high-load rotating machinery. By modeling the rotor-bearing system as an infinite-dimensional constrained Hamiltonian manifold, we couple magnetohydrodynamic field energy, Reynolds lubrication dynamics, and autonomous control penalties into a unified variational framework. Dirac-bracket constraint enforcement guarantees that active magnetic levitation arrays and redundant fluid film interfaces maintain a strict zero-contact operational state. We formally prove Theorem 4.1 (Explicit Friction Collapse), demonstrating that effective macroscopic friction coefficients \mu_{\text{eff}} bound downward to the asymptotic order \mathcal{O}(10^{-5} \text{ to } 10^{-6}).
